export const EMBEDDED_POLICY_MARKDOWN: Record<string, string> = {"OMAYA-Terms-of-Service-v1.5.md":"# Terms of Service\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.5\n\n---\n\nThese Terms of Service (\"**Terms**\") govern your access to and use of the website, mobile application, and services operated under the name **OMAYA.io** by **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**, a private limited company incorporated under Company Law No. 18 of 26 December 2019 of the Federal Republic of Somalia (Registration No. LAG/UBI: 12029035324), with its registered office at Aaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia (\"**OMAYA**,\" \"**OMAYA EXCHANGE**,\" the \"**Company**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\").\n\n**Please read these Terms carefully before using our Services.** They form a binding legal agreement between you and OMAYA. By creating an account, accessing the OMAYA.io website or mobile application, or using any of our Services, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by these Terms and by all policies incorporated into them by reference. **If you do not agree, you must not access or use the Services.**\n\n> **Important — please note:**\n> - Trading and holding digital assets and engaging in foreign exchange carry significant risk, including the risk of losing all of the funds involved. You should read our **Risk Disclosure Statement** before using the Services.\n> - OMAYA does not provide investment, financial, legal, tax, or trading advice. Nothing in the Services is a recommendation to enter into any transaction.\n> - Where OMAYA acts as a **local agent for third-party foreign exchange brokers**, your trading relationship is with that broker and not with OMAYA. See Section 7.\n> - In **peer-to-peer (P2P) trading**, OMAYA is only a facilitator and is not a party to the trade between users. See Section 8.\n\n---\n\n## 1. About OMAYA and These Terms\n\n1.1. OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE is a financial services provider based in Mogadishu, Somalia. Our Services include: exchange of digital assets for local payment methods and vice versa (\"Exchange\"); crypto-to-crypto conversions (\"Swap\"); transfers between local payment providers and wallets (\"MoneyX\"); peer-to-peer trading (\"P2P\"); foreign exchange and currency exchange; remittance and payment services; and acting as a local agent for third-party foreign exchange brokers, in each case as further described in these Terms.\n\n1.2. These Terms apply to all users of the Services, whether accessing through the OMAYA.io website, the OMAYA.io mobile application, or any other channel we make available.\n\n1.3. The following policies are incorporated into and form part of these Terms. By agreeing to these Terms, you also agree to them. Where a specific policy conflicts with these Terms on a matter it governs, that policy prevails on that matter:\n\n- **Privacy Policy**\n- **Cookie Policy**\n- **AML/KYC Policy** (public summary)\n- **Risk Disclosure Statement**\n- **Payment Policy**\n- **Referral Program Terms** (where you participate)\n- **Law Enforcement Request Guidelines**\n\n1.4. We may publish additional product-specific terms, limits, or guidelines for particular features. Where we do, they apply in addition to these Terms.\n\n1.5. **Regulatory status and scope.** OMAYA holds a Commercial Licence issued by the Ministry of Commerce, a licence from the Central Bank of Somalia, and a licence from the Banadir Regional Administration. OMAYA provides the Services only within the scope of the licences, approvals, registrations, exemptions, partnerships, or permissions available to it from time to time. Some Services may be provided through third-party partners, and some Services or features may be unavailable in certain jurisdictions or to certain users.\n\n## 2. Definitions\n\nIn these Terms, unless the context requires otherwise:\n\n- \"**Account**\" means the account you register with OMAYA to access the Services.\n- \"**Authorised User**\" means a person permitted to access or give instructions on an Account on behalf of the Account holder.\n- \"**Beneficial Owner**\" means a natural person who ultimately owns or controls a customer or on whose behalf a transaction is conducted.\n- \"**Broker**\" means a third-party foreign exchange broker with whom OMAYA has a partnership and in respect of whom OMAYA acts as a local agent (see Section 7).\n- \"**Digital Asset**\" means any digital representation of value that can be stored and transferred electronically, including cryptocurrencies such as Bitcoin (BTC), stablecoins such as USDT (Tether), and any other virtual asset supported on the Platform from time to time.\n- \"**Exchange**\" means the service described in Section 6.1.\n- \"**Fiat**\" means government-issued currency that is legal tender in its country of issue.\n- \"**Forex Services**\" means the services described in Section 7.\n- \"**MoneyX**\" means the local payment transfer services described in Section 6.3.\n- \"**P2P Merchant**\" means a user approved by OMAYA to post advertisements and trade as a seller (and, where permitted, buyer) in the P2P market under OMAYA's merchant or verified-seller program.\n- \"**P2P Services**\" means the peer-to-peer trading services described in Section 8.\n- \"**Platform**\" means the OMAYA.io website, mobile application, and related systems through which the Services are provided.\n- \"**Self-Hosted Wallet**\" means an external Digital Asset wallet controlled by a user or third party and not hosted or controlled by OMAYA or another regulated virtual asset service provider.\n- \"**Services**\" means all products, features, and services made available by OMAYA, as described in these Terms.\n- \"**Stablecoin**\" means a Digital Asset designed or marketed to maintain a reference value relative to Fiat, another asset, or a basket of assets.\n- \"**Swap**\" means the crypto-to-crypto conversion service described in Section 6.2.\n- \"**Transaction**\" means any exchange, trade, conversion, transfer, deposit, withdrawal, or remittance carried out through the Services.\n- \"**Travel Rule**\" means legal, regulatory, or industry requirements to collect, transmit, verify, or retain originator and beneficiary information for virtual asset transfers.\n- \"**you**\" or \"**your**\" means the individual or entity using the Services. Where you act on behalf of an entity, you confirm you are authorised to bind that entity, and \"you\" refers to both you and that entity.\n\n## 3. Eligibility\n\n3.1. To use the Services, you must:\n\n(a) be at least **18 years old** and have full legal capacity to enter into a binding contract;  \n(b) not be a resident of, or located in, a jurisdiction where use of the Services is prohibited, or a jurisdiction subject to comprehensive sanctions or designated by the Financial Action Task Force (FATF) as high-risk and subject to a call for action;  \n(c) not be a person or entity subject to sanctions administered by the United Nations, the United States Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC), the European Union, the United Kingdom, the Central Bank of Somalia, or any other applicable authority, nor owned or controlled by, or acting on behalf of, any such person;  \n(d) not have been previously suspended or removed from the Services; and  \n(e) comply with all laws applicable to you in connection with your use of the Services.\n\n3.2. The Services are not offered where prohibited by law. We may restrict or refuse access to any person or in any jurisdiction at our discretion and in accordance with applicable law. You are solely responsible for ensuring that your use of the Services is lawful where you are located.\n\n3.3. You may not use another person's identity, or access the Services through tools intended to disguise your location or circumvent eligibility or geographic controls.\n\n## 4. Your Account\n\n4.1. **Registration.** To use most Services you must register an Account and provide accurate, current, and complete information. You agree to keep this information up to date.\n\n4.2. **One account.** Unless we approve otherwise in writing, you may hold only one Account and may use the Account only for your own benefit and not on behalf of any undisclosed third party.\n\n4.3. **Security.** You are responsible for safeguarding your Account credentials and for all activity that occurs under your Account. You must keep your password and any authentication methods confidential, enable available security features, and notify us immediately at support@omaya.io if you suspect unauthorised access. We are not liable for losses arising from your failure to keep your credentials secure.\n\n4.4. **Accuracy and cooperation.** You authorise us to rely on the instructions and information you provide. We may at any time require you to provide additional information or documentation, and you agree to cooperate promptly with such requests.\n\n4.5. **Corporate accounts.** Where the Account is held by a company, partnership, organisation, trust, foundation, association, or other legal entity, we may require documents and information to verify the entity, its business activity, ownership and control structure, directors, managers, Authorised Users, and Beneficial Owners, together with source of funds, source of wealth, and the purpose of the relationship.\n\n4.6. **Beneficial owners and controllers.** We may require identification and verification of Beneficial Owners, controlling persons, directors, senior managers, and any person who owns, controls, benefits from, or gives instructions in relation to an entity Account.\n\n4.7. **Authority to act.** We may require board resolutions, authorisation letters, powers of attorney, licences, constitutional documents, or other evidence that a person is authorised to open or operate a corporate Account. You confirm that you are duly authorised to act for and bind the entity, which is jointly and severally bound by these Terms.\n\n4.8. **Authorised Users.** A corporate Account holder is responsible for all acts, omissions, instructions, and activity of its Authorised Users, and we may act on instructions from Authorised Users in accordance with the permissions set for the Account.\n\n4.9. **Changes to ownership or control.** You must promptly notify us of any change in beneficial ownership, control, directors, Authorised Users, business activity, licensing status, sanctions status, or other information previously provided. We may refuse, suspend, restrict, or close a corporate Account where we cannot verify the entity, its Beneficial Owners, its source of funds, or its authority to use the Services, or where the entity is outside our risk appetite.\n\n## 5. Identity Verification, KYC, AML and Sanctions\n\n5.1. OMAYA is subject to anti-money laundering and counter-terrorism financing obligations and maintains a compliance program consistent with applicable Somali law (including the Anti-Money Laundering Law and the requirements of the Financial Reporting Center and the Central Bank of Somalia) and international standards.\n\n5.2. As a condition of using the Services, you agree to complete identity verification (\"**KYC**\") and to provide any information and documentation we request to verify your identity, source of funds, source of wealth, and the purpose of your Transactions. We use third-party identity verification and screening providers to perform these checks.\n\n5.3. We may, at our discretion and to the extent permitted or required by law: (a) refuse to open, suspend, restrict, or close an Account; (b) delay, refuse, freeze, reverse, or cancel any Transaction; (c) request further information or documentation; and (d) report activity to, and share information with, competent authorities, where we consider it necessary to comply with our legal obligations, to manage financial crime risk, or to protect OMAYA or others. Where the law prohibits us from disclosing the reason for such action (for example, where doing so would constitute unlawful \"tipping off\"), we may be unable to explain it to you.\n\n5.4. **Virtual asset transfer information and Travel Rule.** For Digital Asset transfers, we may collect, verify, store, transmit, and receive information about the originator, beneficiary, wallet owner, counterparty, and transaction purpose, as required by applicable law, the Travel Rule, payment partners, or our compliance procedures. We may share originator and beneficiary information with other virtual asset service providers, financial institutions, regulators, or law enforcement, and may delay, reject, freeze, return, or cancel a transfer where required information is missing, incomplete, inconsistent, or unacceptable to us.\n\n5.5. **Wallet verification and self-hosted wallets.** We may require you to verify that you own or control an external wallet address before allowing deposits, withdrawals, or transfers. Transfers to or from Self-Hosted Wallets may be subject to enhanced due diligence, ownership checks, limits, delays, or refusal, and we may decline to support a Self-Hosted Wallet where we consider the risk unacceptable.\n\n5.6. **Blockchain analytics and screening.** We may screen wallet addresses, transactions, and blockchain activity using internal tools and third-party analytics providers, and may reject, delay, freeze, return, or report transactions associated with sanctions, darknet markets, mixers, ransomware, scams, stolen funds, terrorist financing, or other activity outside our risk appetite.\n\n5.7. **Enhanced due diligence, PEPs and high-risk factors.** We may apply enhanced due diligence to any user, Account, transaction, wallet, counterparty, jurisdiction, or payment method we consider higher risk. High-risk factors include, without limitation, high-risk or sanctioned jurisdictions, FATF-listed jurisdictions, politically exposed persons, adverse media, unusual or high-volume transaction patterns, complex ownership structures, third-party payments, crypto-mixer exposure, and cross-border transfers. We may request additional documents and evidence, and may refuse onboarding, restrict features, lower limits, delay or reject transactions, or terminate the relationship where we determine the risk is unacceptable, even if the activity is not expressly prohibited by these Terms.\n\n5.8. **Biometric and liveness verification.** Our identity-verification providers may require a facial image or selfie, liveness detection, document authenticity checks, or related biometric verification to confirm your identity and prevent fraud. Such checks are carried out subject to our **Privacy Policy** and applicable law.\n\n5.9. Further detail is set out in our **AML/KYC Policy**.\n\n## 6. Our Services\n\n*In the Services described in this Section, OMAYA acts as principal or operator and is your service provider or counterparty. Different arrangements apply to Forex Services (Section 7), where OMAYA acts only as a local agent, and to P2P Services (Section 8), where OMAYA acts only as a facilitator.*\n\n6.1. **Exchange (Crypto ↔ Local Payment).** OMAYA enables you to buy supported Digital Assets (including BTC and USDT) using supported local payment methods, and to sell supported Digital Assets for payout to supported local payment methods, at the rates we quote at the time of the Transaction.\n\n6.2. **Crypto-to-Crypto Swap.** OMAYA enables you to convert one supported Digital Asset into another (a \"Swap\") at the rates we quote at the time of the Swap. Swap rates are indicative until the Swap is confirmed and may be sourced through third-party liquidity providers or exchanges (see Section 20). You are responsible for selecting the correct assets and networks; once confirmed, a Swap is generally final and irreversible.\n\n6.3. **MoneyX — Local Payment Transfers.** OMAYA enables you to move value between supported local payment providers, banks, mobile money services, e-wallets, and payment applications — for example, from one local wallet to another — subject to verification, limits, fees, availability, and applicable law. The supported channels are shown on the Platform and may be added, removed, suspended, or limited at any time.\n\n(a) **Correct details.** You are solely responsible for providing accurate payment details, including phone numbers, wallet and account numbers, account names, references, and beneficiary information. OMAYA is not responsible for losses, delays, or failed transfers caused by incorrect, incomplete, or incompatible details you provide.  \n(b) **Name matching and third-party payments.** We may require the sending or receiving account name to match the verified name on your Account, and may reject, delay, reverse, or hold any payment involving a third-party account, unmatched name, or unapproved payment source.  \n(c) **Provider delays and outages.** MoneyX depends on third-party banks, mobile money operators, payment processors, and telecom operators. OMAYA is not responsible for delays, outages, rejected transfers, provider errors, or settlement failures caused by these third parties.  \n(d) **Quotes and quote expiry.** Rates may be indicative until confirmed and may expire if payment is not completed in time, if market rates change, or if the transaction is subject to compliance review. We may requote, cancel, or reject a transaction where the original quote is no longer valid.  \n(e) **Failed, pending, reversed, or duplicate payments.** We may delay completion, request evidence, return funds where possible, deduct duplicate credits, or restrict the Account to correct an issue and manage risk. A screenshot, receipt, or notification does not guarantee that funds have been finally received and cleared.\n\n6.4. **Currency Exchange.** OMAYA provides currency exchange and conversion between supported currencies at the rates we quote at the time of the Transaction.\n\n6.5. **Remittance and Payments.** OMAYA provides remittance and payment services enabling you to send and receive funds through supported channels, subject to verification, limits, and applicable law.\n\n6.6. **Balances and Custody.**\n\n(a) Where the Services allow you to hold Fiat or Digital Asset balances, those balances are held by us for you. Holding a balance with OMAYA is not a bank deposit and is not insured or guaranteed by any deposit protection, investor compensation, or government guarantee scheme unless expressly required by applicable law. Unless we expressly agree otherwise in writing, balances do not earn interest.  \n(b) **Safeguarding.** We use reasonable administrative, technical, operational, and security measures designed to safeguard balances we hold. Where required by applicable law or our internal policies, we may hold client Fiat funds separately from our own operating funds.  \n(c) **Custody structure.** Digital Assets may be held in hot, warm, cold, omnibus, segregated, or third-party custodian wallets selected by us. Unless we expressly state otherwise, Digital Assets may be held in omnibus wallets together with assets of other users.  \n(d) **No unauthorised use.** Unless expressly disclosed to you and permitted by applicable law, we will not sell, lend, pledge, rehypothecate, or otherwise use your assets for our own trading, lending, investment, or speculative purposes.  \n(e) **Custody and insolvency risk.** Custody of Digital Assets involves operational and technological risks, including private-key compromise, cyber-attacks, wallet or network failure, smart-contract vulnerabilities, and third-party custodian failure.\n\n6.7. **Availability and changes.** We may add, modify, suspend, or discontinue any Service, feature, or supported asset, and may set or change limits at any time, acting reasonably and in accordance with applicable law.\n\n## 7. Forex Services — OMAYA as Local Agent\n\n**This Section governs OMAYA's role in connection with foreign exchange and contract-for-difference (\"CFD\") trading services provided by third-party Brokers.**\n\n7.1. **OMAYA's role is limited to that of a local agent.** In connection with the Forex Services, OMAYA acts **solely as a local agent and introducer** for one or more Brokers.\n\n7.2. **What OMAYA is not, and does not do.** In connection with the Forex Services, OMAYA is **not** the Broker and is **not** a party or counterparty to any trade.\n\n7.3. **Your trading relationship is with the Broker.** Your trading account, your trading agreement, and all trading activity are between **you and the Broker** and are governed exclusively by the Broker's own terms, agreements, policies, and risk disclosures.\n\n7.4. **No liability for the Broker.** To the maximum extent permitted by law, OMAYA is **not responsible or liable** for the acts, omissions, or performance of any Broker.\n\n7.5. **Funds handling.** Where OMAYA facilitates a transfer between you and a Broker, OMAYA acts only as a **local payment conduit**.\n\n7.6. **Risk.** Foreign exchange and CFD trading is highly speculative, involves substantial risk, and can result in the loss of all funds and, due to leverage, losses exceeding the amount you deposit. You should not trade unless you fully understand and can afford these risks. See our **Risk Disclosure Statement**.\n\n## 8. Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Trading\n\n**In connection with P2P Services, OMAYA acts only as a facilitator and is not a party or counterparty to the trade between users.**\n\n8.1. **P2P Services.** Where OMAYA makes P2P Services available, you may buy or sell supported Digital Assets with other users using supported payment methods, subject to the limits, eligibility, fees, and procedures shown on the Platform.\n\n8.2. **OMAYA's role.** In P2P Services, OMAYA acts only as a platform provider, technology facilitator, and, where applicable, escrow or asset-locking facilitator.\n\n## 9. Orders, Pricing, Execution and Settlement\n\n9.1. **Quotes and pricing.** Prices, exchange rates, and quotes displayed on the Platform are indicative and may change rapidly.\n\n9.2. **Authorisation and finality.** **Transactions involving Digital Assets and blockchain transfers are generally irreversible and cannot be cancelled, reversed, or recovered once submitted.**\n\n## 10. Digital Assets: Forks, Airdrops, Migrations and Delisting\n\nOMAYA may decide whether and how to support forks, airdrops, upgrades, token swaps, migrations, or delistings.\n\n## 11. Deposits and Withdrawals\n\nYou may fund your Account and make withdrawals through the methods we make available, subject to verification, limits, fees, and applicable law.\n\n## 12. Security, Device Controls and Fraud Prevention\n\nWe may monitor and process security-related information to protect users and the Platform, and we may delay or block Transactions where we suspect fraud or scams.\n\n## 13. Fees, Charges, Set-Off and Negative Balances\n\nYou agree to pay all applicable fees, spreads, and charges for the Services, as published on the Platform or in our **Payment Policy**.\n\n## 14. Promotions, Rewards and Referral Controls\n\nPromotions are discretionary and may be subject to separate terms, eligibility rules, and anti-abuse controls.\n\n## 15. Risk Disclosure and No Advice\n\nOMAYA does not provide investment, financial, legal, tax, or trading advice. A full description of risks is set out in our **Risk Disclosure Statement**.\n\n## 16. Prohibited Uses and Restricted Activities\n\nYou must not use the Services to breach laws or sanctions, engage in financial crime, or commit fraud, manipulation, or other harmful activity.\n\n## 17. Suspension, Restriction, Closure, Account Deletion and Dormant Accounts\n\nWe may suspend or close Accounts to comply with law, manage risk, or address suspected fraud or breaches.\n\n## 18. Intellectual Property and Licence\n\nAll intellectual property rights in the Platform and the Services are owned by or licensed to OMAYA.\n\n## 19. Mobile Application Terms\n\nThe App is licensed, not sold, to you; additional app-store terms apply.\n\n## 20. Third-Party Providers, Partners and Links\n\nThe Services may rely on third parties; we are not responsible for third-party services except as expressly stated in these Terms.\n\n## 21. Privacy and Data Protection\n\nOur collection and use of personal data is described in our **Privacy Policy**.\n\n## 22. Electronic Communications and Notices\n\nYou consent to receiving communications from us electronically.\n\n## 23. Taxes and Information Reporting\n\nYou are responsible for determining and paying any taxes that apply to you.\n\n## 24. Disclaimers\n\nThe Services are provided **\"as is\" and \"as available\"** to the maximum extent permitted by law.\n\n## 25. Limitation of Liability\n\nTo the maximum extent permitted by law, OMAYA’s liability is limited as described in these Terms.\n\n## 26. Indemnification\n\nYou agree to indemnify OMAYA for claims arising from your use or breach.\n\n## 27. Governing Law, Complaints and Dispute Resolution\n\nThese Terms are governed by the laws of the Federal Republic of Somalia.\n\n## 28. Changes to These Terms\n\nWe may amend these Terms from time to time.\n\n## 29. General Provisions\n\nStandard contract provisions apply, including severability and force majeure.\n\n## 30. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- General and support: support@omaya.io  \n- Legal: legal@omaya.io  \n- Compliance: compliance@omaya.io\n\n---\n\n*These Terms of Service should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel familiar with the laws of Somalia and the jurisdictions in which OMAYA's customers are located before publication.*\n","OMAYA-Privacy-Policy-v1.2.md":"# Privacy Policy\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.2\n\n---\n\nThis Privacy Policy explains how **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**, a private limited company incorporated under Company Law No. 18 of 26 December 2019 of the Federal Republic of Somalia (Registration No. LAG/UBI: 12029035324), with its registered office at Aaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia (\"**OMAYA**,\" \"**OMAYA EXCHANGE**,\" \"**OMAYA.io**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\"), collects, uses, shares, and protects your personal data when you use our website, mobile application, and services (the \"**Services**\").\n\nOMAYA is the **data controller** responsible for your personal data. This Privacy Policy should be read together with our **Terms of Service** and our **Cookie Policy**. If you do not agree with this Privacy Policy, you should not use the Services.\n\n**Applicable data-protection law.** We process personal data primarily in accordance with applicable Somali law, including the Data Protection Act, 2023 (Law No. 005) and any regulations or guidance issued by the Somalia Data Protection Authority, together with our obligations under Somali financial and anti-money-laundering law. Where you are located in another region, additional data-protection laws may also apply to you, as described in Section 15.\n\nIf you have any questions or wish to exercise your rights, contact us at **privacy@omaya.io**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Personal Data We Collect\n\nWe collect the following categories of personal data.\n\n### 1.1 Information you provide to us\n\n- **Identity and contact information:** full name, date and place of birth, nationality, residential address, email address, and phone number.\n- **Identity verification (KYC) information:** identity documents (such as passport, national identity card, or driving licence), proof of address, and related photographs or scans.\n- **Biometric and liveness data:** a facial image or selfie, liveness-check data, and document-authenticity data, collected through our identity-verification provider to confirm your identity and prevent fraud. These checks are used only for identity verification, fraud prevention, and compliance. Where biometric verification is required for KYC, refusing it may prevent us from opening or maintaining your Account or providing certain Services. Our verification provider may process this information on our behalf, and OMAYA generally receives verification results, risk indicators, and supporting records rather than raw biometric templates. Where we rely on your consent for biometric processing, we seek it separately at the point of verification (see Section 1.4).\n- **Financial and transaction information:** payment details (including, where you make card payments, limited payment-card information processed by our payment providers — we do not store full card details), bank and mobile-money account details, wallet addresses, transaction history, and information about your source of funds and source of wealth.\n- **Account and profile information:** username, account settings, and preferences.\n- **P2P information:** advertisements, order details, in-app chat messages, payment proofs, and dispute evidence. If you are a P2P Merchant, we may also collect additional verification information, security-deposit or reserve details, and performance metrics such as completion and release rates.\n- **Communications:** messages to our support team, complaints, and survey or feedback responses.\n- **Corporate account information:** entity details, directors, beneficial owners, authorised users, and supporting documents.\n- **Privacy choices and consent records:** records of your consents, permissions, opt-outs, and withdrawals, such as for marketing, cookies, location, and biometric processing.\n\n### 1.2 Information we collect automatically\n\n- **Device and technical information:** device and browser type, operating system, device identifiers, and app version.\n- **Network and location information:** IP address, approximate location, and, where you grant permission, more precise location.\n- **Usage information:** features and pages used, log data, and session and login activity.\n- **Security and fraud-prevention signals:** device fingerprint, risk signals, and behavioural patterns used to detect fraud and protect accounts.\n- **Diagnostics and notifications:** analytics, crash reports, diagnostics, performance and error logs, and, where you enable push notifications, device tokens and notification delivery information.\n- **Cookies and similar technologies:** as described in our **Cookie Policy**.\n\n### 1.3 Blockchain and transaction data\n\nDigital Asset transactions are recorded on public blockchains. We may collect and analyse wallet addresses and on-chain transaction data, including by using blockchain-analytics tools, for compliance, security, and fraud-prevention purposes.\n\n### 1.4 Information we receive from third parties\n\nWe may receive personal data about you from: identity-verification and screening providers (including **Sumsub**, which performs identity verification, biometric and document checks, and sanctions, PEP, and watchlist screening); sanctions, politically-exposed-person, and adverse-media data sources; blockchain-analytics providers; payment, banking, and mobile-money partners; third-party sign-in providers (where you choose to register or log in using them); our affiliates; and publicly available sources.\n\n## 2. How We Use Your Personal Data\n\nWe use your personal data to:\n\n- provide, operate, and maintain the Services and process your Transactions;\n- create, verify, and manage your Account, including identity verification and onboarding;\n- meet our anti-money-laundering and counter-terrorism-financing obligations, including KYC, sanctions and PEP screening, transaction monitoring, and the Travel Rule;\n- detect, prevent, and investigate fraud, scams, and security threats, and manage risk;\n- comply with our legal and regulatory obligations and respond to requests from regulators, the Financial Reporting Center, the Central Bank of Somalia, and other competent authorities;\n- secure the Platform and your Account;\n- provide customer support and handle complaints;\n- improve, personalise, and develop the Services;\n- send you service, transaction, security, and legal communications, and, where permitted, marketing communications; and\n- enforce our Terms of Service and protect our rights, property, and users.\n\n## 3. Legal Bases for Processing\n\nWhere data-protection law (such as the EU and UK General Data Protection Regulation) applies, we rely on the following legal bases:\n\n- **Performance of a contract** — to provide the Services you request and operate your Account.\n- **Compliance with legal obligations** — including anti-money-laundering, counter-terrorism-financing, sanctions, tax, and record-keeping requirements.\n- **Legitimate interests** — including securing our Platform, preventing fraud, improving the Services, and direct marketing where permitted, balanced against your rights and interests.\n- **Consent** — for certain marketing, certain cookies, and where otherwise required; you may withdraw consent at any time.\n- **Biometric and special-category data** — we process biometric data (for identity verification) where it is necessary for compliance with our legal obligations and/or on the basis of your explicit consent, and on grounds of substantial public interest where applicable.\n\nThe table below maps our main processing purposes to their legal bases. Where more than one basis applies, we rely on each as relevant:\n\n| Purpose | Legal basis |\n|---|---|\n| Creating and operating your Account | Performance of a contract |\n| KYC, AML, sanctions and PEP screening | Legal obligation; substantial public interest; explicit consent where required (e.g., biometrics) |\n| Processing Transactions | Performance of a contract; legal obligation |\n| Fraud prevention and security | Legitimate interests; legal obligation |\n| Travel Rule compliance | Legal obligation |\n| Customer support | Performance of a contract; legitimate interests |\n| Marketing | Consent, or legitimate interests where permitted |\n| Improving the Services | Legitimate interests |\n| Legal claims and enforcement | Legitimate interests; legal obligation |\n\n## 4. How We Share Your Personal Data\n\n**We do not sell your personal data.** We may share it with:\n\n- **Service providers and processors** acting on our behalf under contract, including identity-verification and screening providers (such as Sumsub), hosting and IT providers, analytics and communications providers, and customer-support providers;\n- **Payment, banking, and mobile-money partners, liquidity providers, and cryptocurrency exchanges**, to process or route your Transactions;\n- **Partner foreign exchange Brokers**, where you use our Forex Services, to facilitate your onboarding, compliance vetting, and the settlement of local deposits and withdrawals;\n- **Blockchain-analytics and fraud-prevention providers**;\n- **Other virtual asset service providers and financial institutions**, where necessary to comply with the Travel Rule or to process a transfer. To comply with the Travel Rule, we may be required to transmit information such as the originator's name, account or wallet identifier, and address or identification number, together with the beneficiary's name and account or wallet identifier, to the counterparty provider;\n- **Regulators, the Financial Reporting Center, the Central Bank of Somalia, law enforcement, courts, and other authorities**, where required or permitted by law;\n- **Professional advisers**, such as legal, audit, and accounting advisers;\n- **Parties to a corporate transaction**, such as a merger, acquisition, or reorganisation; and\n- **Other parties with your consent** or at your direction.\n\nWe require our service providers to protect your personal data and to use it only for the purposes for which it is shared. For more information about how we handle law-enforcement and government requests, see our **Law Enforcement Request Guidelines**.\n\n## 5. Third-Party Sign-In and Platform Integrations\n\nWhere you choose to register or log in using a third-party sign-in provider, we receive certain information from that provider (such as your name, email address, and an account identifier), as permitted by your settings with that provider. Your use of any third-party sign-in or account is also governed by that provider's own terms and privacy policy. Where we use third-party platform services, we handle any personal data we receive in accordance with this Privacy Policy and the applicable requirements of those platforms.\n\n## 6. International Data Transfers\n\nWe are based in Somalia and may transfer and store personal data in Somalia and in other countries where we or our service providers operate. Our service providers — including our identity-verification provider, hosting and analytics providers, blockchain-analytics providers, and payment partners — may process personal data in the European Economic Area, the United Kingdom, and other countries where they or their sub-processors operate. Where we transfer the personal data of individuals located in the EEA or the UK to a country that does not have an adequacy decision, we use appropriate safeguards — such as standard contractual clauses or the UK international data-transfer addendum — or rely on a permitted exception. You may contact us at **privacy@omaya.io** to request further information about the safeguards we use for international transfers.\n\n## 7. Automated Decision-Making and Profiling\n\nWe use automated systems and automated decision-making for fraud detection, transaction and sanctions screening, risk scoring, and compliance. These processes may result in a Transaction or Account being delayed, refused, restricted, or closed. Where a decision that produces legal or similarly significant effects is based solely on automated processing, you may request human review — except where the processing is necessary for entering into or performing a contract with you, is required for compliance with our legal obligations (such as anti-money-laundering requirements), or is based on your explicit consent.\n\n## 8. Marketing Communications\n\nService, transaction, security, and legal communications form part of the Services, and you may be unable to opt out of them while you hold an Account. We may also send marketing or promotional messages by email, SMS, messaging apps, or push notification where permitted. You can opt out of marketing communications at any time using the unsubscribe option or by contacting us; opting out will not affect service, transaction, security, or legal communications.\n\n## 9. Cookies and Similar Technologies\n\nWe use cookies and similar technologies to operate the Platform, remember your preferences, improve the Services, and support security and analytics. For details, and to manage your choices, please see our **Cookie Policy**.\n\n## 10. Data Retention\n\nWe keep personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy and to meet our legal, regulatory, and record-keeping obligations. Indicative retention periods are:\n\n- **Identity, KYC, and transaction records:** at least five (5) years after the end of your relationship with us or after the relevant Transaction, as required by anti-money-laundering and record-keeping rules.\n- **Compliance, screening, and suspicious-activity records:** at least five (5) years.\n- **Account and communications records:** for the duration of your relationship with us and a reasonable period afterward.\n- **Marketing data:** until you withdraw consent or object, or until it is no longer needed.\n- **Biometric and liveness records:** retained only for as long as necessary for identity verification, fraud prevention, AML/CFT compliance, legal claims, and audit, unless a longer period is required or permitted by law.\n- **Security, device, and fraud-prevention logs:** for the period necessary for security and fraud-prevention purposes.\n\nAfter the applicable period, we delete or anonymise your personal data, subject to copies that may remain in backups for a limited period until overwritten (see Section 13).\n\n## 11. Data Security\n\nWe maintain technical and organisational measures designed to protect personal data, including encryption, access controls, and monitoring. However, no method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security. If we become aware of a personal-data breach, we will assess it promptly and, where required by applicable law (including the Data Protection Act, 2023), notify affected users and/or the competent authority.\n\n## 12. Your Privacy Rights\n\nThe following rights apply to the extent required by the data-protection law that applies to you, and may vary depending on where you live:\n\n- **Access** — to obtain confirmation of, and a copy of, the personal data we hold about you;\n- **Rectification** — to correct inaccurate or incomplete data;\n- **Erasure** — to request deletion of your data (the \"right to be forgotten\");\n- **Restriction** — to restrict our processing in certain circumstances;\n- **Data portability** — to receive certain data in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format;\n- **Objection** — to object to processing based on legitimate interests and to direct marketing;\n- **Withdrawal of consent** — where processing is based on consent;\n- **Automated decisions** — not to be subject to solely automated decisions producing legal or similarly significant effects, subject to the exceptions in Section 7; and\n- **Complaint** — to lodge a complaint with your local data-protection authority.\n\nThese rights are subject to limitations. In particular, we are required to retain certain records (such as KYC and transaction records) for anti-money-laundering, tax, and legal purposes, and may be unable to delete them even if you request erasure.\n\nTo exercise any of these rights, contact us at **privacy@omaya.io**. We may need to verify your identity before responding. We will respond within the time required by applicable law (for example, within one month under the GDPR, which may be extended for complex requests).\n\n## 13. Account Closure and Data Deletion\n\nYou may close your Account as described in our Terms of Service. You may also request deletion of your Account and personal data:\n\n- through the **in-app account-deletion option** in the OMAYA.io mobile application; or\n- through our **account-deletion page** at https://omaya.io/delete-account, which is also linked in the App and on our website.\n\nAccount closure and account deletion are different. Closure ends your access to the Services; deletion involves removing or deactivating personal data from our active systems. Following a deletion request, we will delete or anonymise your personal data, **except** for data we are required or permitted to retain for the periods set out in Section 10 (including KYC, transaction, compliance, tax, and legal records). Deletion may be delayed or refused where your Account has pending Transactions, remaining balances, unresolved disputes, investigations, or legal holds. Copies of deleted data may remain in our backups and disaster-recovery systems for a limited period until they are overwritten in the ordinary course. If those systems are ever restored, we apply controls designed to ensure that data you asked us to delete is not reinstated into our active systems and is re-deleted.\n\n## 14. Children's Privacy\n\nThe Services are intended only for individuals aged 18 or over. We do not knowingly collect personal data from anyone under 18. If we become aware that we have collected personal data from a person under 18, we will delete it.\n\n## 15. Region-Specific Information\n\n### 15.1 European Economic Area and United Kingdom\n\nIf you are located in the EEA or the UK, OMAYA is the data controller of your personal data; the legal bases on which we process it are set out in Section 3; your rights are set out in Section 12; and information about international transfers is in Section 6. You have the right to lodge a complaint with your local data-protection authority (in the EEA) or with the Information Commissioner's Office (in the UK). Where required by applicable law, OMAYA will appoint an EU and/or UK representative and will publish the representative's contact details.\n\n### 15.2 California\n\nThis section applies only where the California Consumer Privacy Act, as amended, applies to OMAYA and to your personal information. If you are a California resident, we collect the categories of personal information described in Section 1 (which may include identifiers, financial and commercial information, internet and device activity, geolocation, and sensitive personal information such as government identifiers and biometric information) for the purposes described in Section 2, and we use sensitive personal information only for permitted purposes such as identity verification, security, and compliance. **We do not sell your personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising.** You have the right to know about, access, delete, and correct your personal information, to limit the use of sensitive personal information, to opt out of any sale or sharing, and not to be discriminated against for exercising your rights; you may use an authorised agent to make a request, and we may verify your identity before responding. Because we do not sell or share personal information for cross-context behavioural advertising, this is not a sale or share opt-out; however, where required by applicable law, we honour Global Privacy Control and similar opt-out preference signals as a request to disable non-essential cookies (see our **Cookie Policy**). To exercise these rights, contact us at **privacy@omaya.io**.\n\n### 15.3 Other regions\n\nYou may have additional rights under the data-protection laws that apply where you live. Please contact us to find out more.\n\n## 16. Changes to This Privacy Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version on the Platform and update the \"Last Updated\" date, and where the changes are material we will take reasonable steps to notify you. Your continued use of the Services after the changes take effect indicates your acknowledgement of the updated Privacy Policy.\n\n## 17. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\nOMAYA has appointed a privacy contact responsible for handling privacy and data-protection requests.\n\n- Privacy and data-protection enquiries and requests: **privacy@omaya.io**\n- General and support: **support@omaya.io**\n","OMAYA-Cookie-Policy-v1.1.md":"# Cookie Policy\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThis Cookie Policy explains how **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**, \"**OMAYA**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\") uses cookies and similar technologies on our website and mobile application (the \"**Platform**\"). It should be read together with our **Privacy Policy**, which explains how we handle personal data more generally.\n\nWe use strictly necessary cookies to operate the Platform and keep it secure. Where required by law, we will ask for your consent before setting functional, analytics, performance, or marketing cookies, and you can change or withdraw your choices at any time.\n\n---\n\n## 1. What Are Cookies and Similar Technologies?\n\nCookies are small text files placed on your device when you visit a website. We also use similar technologies, including:\n\n- **Pixels and web beacons** — small pieces of code that help us understand activity on the Platform;\n- **Local storage** — data stored by your browser or app to remember information between sessions;\n- **Software development kits (SDKs)** — code in our mobile app that supports functionality, analytics, and security; and\n- **Device identifiers** — identifiers associated with your device, used mainly in the app.\n\nIn this Policy, we refer to all of these as \"**cookies**.\"\n\n## 2. How We Use Cookies\n\nWe use cookies for the following purposes:\n\n| Category | Purpose | Consent |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Strictly necessary** | Security, authentication, fraud prevention, session management, and load balancing. These are required for the Platform to work and for keeping your account secure. | Always active; cannot be switched off |\n| **Functional** | Remembering your preferences and settings, such as language and display choices. | Set with consent where required |\n| **Analytics / performance** | Understanding how the Platform is used, measuring performance, and diagnosing errors so we can improve the Services. | Set with consent where required |\n| **Marketing** | Measuring and improving the effectiveness of our own marketing and campaigns — for example, understanding whether a visit led to a sign-up. | Set only with your consent |\n\nWe do not use cookies to sell your personal information.\n\nThe specific cookies and similar technologies we use are listed and kept up to date in our cookie settings tool. The following table is illustrative of the types of cookies we use; the live list may differ:\n\n| Cookie / technology | Provider | Category | Purpose | Duration |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Session / authentication token | OMAYA.io | Strictly necessary | Login and session security | Session |\n| Language and display preference | OMAYA.io | Functional | Remember your settings | Up to 12 months |\n| Analytics identifier | Analytics provider | Analytics / performance | Measure website and app usage | Up to 13 months |\n| Fraud / device identifier | Security provider | Strictly necessary (security) | Fraud prevention and account security | 12–24 months |\n\nThe specific cookies, SDKs, and similar technologies we use may change over time, and we will keep the current list in our cookie banner or settings tool.\n\n## 3. First-Party and Third-Party Cookies\n\nSome cookies are set by us (\"first-party cookies\"). Others are set by third parties that provide services on the Platform (\"third-party cookies\"), such as analytics providers, third-party sign-in providers (where you choose to register or log in using them), and security and fraud-prevention providers. These third parties may process information in accordance with their own privacy and cookie policies, which we encourage you to review.\n\n## 4. Cookies in Our Mobile App\n\nOur mobile application uses SDKs, local storage, and device identifiers to support core functionality, security and fraud prevention, analytics, and, where you consent, marketing measurement.\n\n## 5. How Long Cookies Last\n\n- **Session cookies** are temporary and are deleted when you close your browser or app.\n- **Persistent cookies** remain on your device for a set period or until you delete them.\n\n## 6. Your Choices and How to Manage Cookies\n\nYou can control cookies in several ways:\n\n- **Cookie settings.** Our cookie banner and settings tool let you **accept all** non-essential cookies, **reject all** non-essential cookies, or **manage your choices by category**, and change or withdraw your consent at any time. You can manage your cookie choices at https://omaya.io/cookie-settings.\n- **Browser settings.** Most browsers let you block or delete cookies and notify you when a cookie is set.\n- **Device settings.** On mobile devices, you can reset or limit your advertising identifier and manage app permissions.\n- **Analytics and marketing opt-outs.** You can decline analytics and marketing cookies through our cookie settings, where available.\n\nPlease note that if you block strictly necessary cookies, parts of the Platform may not function properly, and we may be unable to keep your account secure.\n\n**Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control.** Some browsers and devices send opt-out preference signals such as Global Privacy Control (GPC) or \"Do Not Track\" (DNT). Where required by applicable law, we treat a GPC signal as a valid request to disable non-essential (analytics and marketing) cookies.\n\n## 7. Consent\n\nWhere required by applicable law, we set non-essential cookies only with your consent, which we request through our cookie banner or settings tool. You can withdraw or change your consent at any time using those settings.\n\n## 8. Changes to This Cookie Policy\n\nWe may update this Cookie Policy from time to time. We will post the updated version on the Platform and update the \"Last Updated\" date.\n\n## 9. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- Privacy and data-protection enquiries: **privacy@omaya.io**  \n- General and support: **support@omaya.io**\n\n---\n\n*This Cookie Policy should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel.*\n","OMAYA-AML-KYC-Policy-v1.1.md":"# AML/KYC Policy\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThis AML/KYC Policy describes how **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**, \"**OMAYA**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\") prevents money laundering, terrorism financing, and other financial crime, and how we verify the identity of our customers. It is a public summary of OMAYA's internal Anti-Money Laundering and Counter-Terrorism Financing (AML/CFT) Policies and Procedures and forms part of our **Terms of Service**. It applies to all users of our website, mobile application, and services (the \"**Services**\").\n\nBecause financial crime controls must remain effective, this Policy describes our approach at a general level and does not disclose the internal thresholds, scoring rules, detection scenarios, or procedures that would undermine those controls.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Our Commitment\n\nOMAYA has **zero tolerance** for money laundering, terrorism financing, proliferation financing, sanctions evasion, fraud, and other financial crime. We are committed to operating with integrity and in full compliance with applicable law, and we apply a **risk-based approach** to identifying, assessing, mitigating, and managing these risks.\n\n## 2. Regulatory Status and Framework\n\nOMAYA holds a Commercial Licence issued by the Ministry of Commerce, a licence from the Central Bank of Somalia, and a licence from the Banadir Regional Administration.\n\nOur AML/CFT program is designed to comply with applicable **Somali law**, and we align our program with recognised **international standards**, including the recommendations of the Financial Action Task Force (FATF).\n\n## 3. Governance and Oversight\n\n- our **Board of Directors** has ultimate oversight and approves our AML/CFT policy;\n- we appoint a **Money Laundering Reporting Officer (MLRO)**; and\n- we operate a \"**three lines of defence**\" model.\n\n## 4. Risk-Based Approach and Customer Risk Rating\n\nWe classify customers and relationships into risk categories (for example, **low, standard, medium, high, or prohibited**) based on factors including customer type, geography, product use, transaction behaviour, sanctions and PEP exposure, source of funds and source of wealth, and delivery channel.\n\n## 5. Customer Due Diligence (KYC)\n\nDepending on risk, we apply **Simplified**, **Standard**, or **Enhanced** due diligence.\n\nAs part of KYC, we may require:\n\n- **Identity information**\n- **Identity documents**\n- **Verification checks** (document-authenticity, facial-image, liveness checks)\n- **Purpose and activity information**\n- **Source of funds and source of wealth** information\n\n## 6. Enhanced Due Diligence (EDD)\n\nWe apply EDD to higher-risk customers and activity.\n\n## 7. Sanctions Compliance\n\nWe screen customers and transactions against applicable sanctions lists and may freeze assets or block transactions where required.\n\n## 8. Politically Exposed Persons (PEPs)\n\nWe screen for PEPs and apply EDD and senior-management approval where relevant.\n\n## 9. Transaction Monitoring\n\nWe monitor activity to detect unusual transactions and potential financial crime and may reject, delay, or investigate transactions as needed.\n\n## 10. Digital Asset and Crypto Compliance\n\nWe use **blockchain-analytics tools** to screen wallet addresses and transactions, and we may apply controls to transfers involving **self-hosted wallets** and comply with **Travel Rule** requirements.\n\n## 11. Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Controls\n\nWe apply additional controls to P2P trading and may monitor P2P chat and evidence for compliance and fraud purposes.\n\n## 12. Reliance on Third Parties and Partner Due Diligence\n\nWe perform risk-based due diligence on partners (payment providers, banks, brokers, and other service providers).\n\n## 13. Suspicious Activity and Regulatory Reporting\n\nWhere required, we report suspicious activity to the **Financial Reporting Center (FRC)** and cooperate with authorities. We may be legally prohibited from informing you of reports or investigations (\"tipping off\").\n\n## 14. Prohibited Customers and Activities\n\nWe do not establish or maintain relationships with sanctioned persons, anonymous customers, shell banks, or customers who refuse required information.\n\n## 15. Record-Keeping\n\nWe retain records for the periods required by applicable law (generally **at least five (5) years**).\n\n## 16. Account Restrictions, Refusal, and Closure\n\nWe may refuse onboarding, restrict features, delay or freeze transactions, or close accounts to comply with law and manage risk.\n\n## 17. Your Responsibilities\n\nYou must provide accurate information, complete verification, use payment accounts in your own name (unless approved otherwise), and cooperate with compliance checks.\n\n## 18. Program Governance, Training and Review\n\nWe train relevant personnel, apply controls, and test and review our program periodically.\n\n## 19. Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this AML/KYC Policy from time to time.\n\n## 20. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- Compliance and AML/KYC enquiries: **compliance@omaya.io**  \n- General and support: **support@omaya.io**\n\n---\n\n*This public AML/KYC Policy is a summary and should be reviewed by OMAYA's MLRO and qualified legal counsel before publication.*\n","OMAYA-Risk-Disclosure-Statement-v1.1.md":"# Risk Disclosure Statement\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThis Risk Disclosure Statement describes some of the risks of using the services of **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**, \"**OMAYA**,\" \"**we**,\" \"**us**,\" or \"**our**\"). It forms part of our **Terms of Service** and should be read together with them.\n\n> **Important — please read carefully. Digital assets are high-risk.**\n> - **You could lose all of the money you use to buy, sell, hold, swap, or transfer digital assets.**\n> - Trading foreign exchange is also high-risk, and because of leverage you can lose **more than you deposit**.\n> - **Only use funds you can afford to lose.**\n> - **OMAYA does not provide investment, financial, legal, tax, or trading advice.**\n\n---\n\n## 1. No Advice and No Guarantee\n\nOMAYA does not provide investment, financial, legal, tax, or trading advice, and does not assess whether any product or transaction is suitable or appropriate for you.\n\n## 2. You May Lose Your Money\n\nThe value of digital assets and currencies can fall as well as rise, sometimes sharply and without warning, and you may lose some or all of the funds involved.\n\n## 3. Do Not Use Borrowed or Essential Funds\n\nYou should not borrow money, or use emergency funds, customer funds, business operating funds, or funds you need for living expenses, to trade or hold digital assets or to trade foreign exchange.\n\n## 4. Risks of Digital Assets (Cryptocurrency)\n\n- **Volatility**\n- **Liquidity**\n- **Irreversibility and wrong network**\n- **Technology and network risk**\n- **Network fees**\n- **Market integrity**\n- **Issuer or project failure**\n- **Security**\n\n## 5. Custody and Insolvency Risk\n\nCustody involves operational, legal, insolvency, and third-party risks.\n\n## 6. Stablecoin Risks\n\nStablecoins (such as USDT) are digital assets and are **not** the same as cash or bank deposits.\n\n## 7. Forks, Delisting, and Restricted or Unsupported Assets\n\nOMAYA may suspend, delist, or cease supporting an asset for legal, regulatory, liquidity, security, or risk reasons.\n\n## 8. Risks of Crypto-to-Crypto Swaps\n\nSwap quotes and outputs may change rapidly and can be rejected or re-priced due to liquidity, slippage, network fees, or compliance review.\n\n## 9. Foreign Exchange (Forex) and Leverage Risks\n\nForex and CFD trading is highly speculative and can result in losses exceeding your deposit. OMAYA acts only as a local agent for third-party brokers.\n\n## 10. MoneyX, Remittance, and Local Payment Risks\n\nTransfers depend on third parties (banks, mobile money, payment providers) and may be delayed, held, refused, or reversed for compliance or fraud reasons.\n\n## 11. Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Trading Risks\n\nIn P2P trading you deal directly with other users; OMAYA is not the buyer, seller, or guarantor.\n\n## 12. Compliance Holds, Sanctions, and Account Restrictions\n\nYour Account or transactions may be delayed, refused, frozen, returned, restricted, reversed, closed, or reported as a result of AML/KYC, sanctions, fraud, or law-enforcement requirements.\n\n## 13. Platform and Operational Risks\n\nThe Platform may be unavailable and data may contain errors that require correction or reversal where permitted by Terms and law.\n\n## 14. Security, Fraud, and Scam Risks\n\nBe alert to phishing and impersonation. OMAYA staff will never ask for your password, full OTP/2FA codes, recovery phrases, or private keys.\n\n## 15. Regulatory and Legal Risks\n\nLaws and regulations may change and can affect availability or legality of Services.\n\n## 16. No Insurance, Compensation, or Ombudsman\n\nBalances held with OMAYA are generally not protected by deposit insurance or compensation schemes.\n\n## 17. Tax Risks\n\nYou are responsible for your tax obligations.\n\n## 18. Third-Party and Partner Risks\n\nServices rely on third parties; OMAYA is not responsible for their acts or solvency except as expressly stated.\n\n## 19. Acknowledgement\n\nBy using the Services, you acknowledge that you have read and understood this Risk Disclosure Statement and accept the risks.\n\n## 20. Contact Us\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as OMAYA.io)  \nAaran Plaza, Taleh, Hodan District, Mogadishu, Somalia\n\n- General and support: **support@omaya.io**\n\n---\n\n*This Risk Disclosure Statement should be reviewed by qualified legal counsel before publication.*\n","OMAYA-Law-Enforcement-Request-Guidelines-v1.1.md":"# Law Enforcement Request Guidelines\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThese guidelines explain how **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**) receives and responds to law enforcement and regulatory requests relating to our Services.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Scope\n\nWe cooperate with lawful requests from competent authorities where we are legally permitted and required to do so, consistent with applicable law and our privacy obligations.\n\n## 2. How to Submit a Request\n\nRequests should be sent from an official government or regulatory email domain and include:\n\n- The requesting agency and jurisdiction\n- Relevant case or reference numbers\n- Specific data sought and time period\n- Legal basis for the request\n- Contact details for the authorised officer\n\n## 3. User Notice\n\nWhere permitted by law, we may notify affected users before disclosing information, unless prohibited or where notice could compromise an investigation.\n\n## 4. Emergency Requests\n\nFor imminent threat-to-life situations, clearly mark the request as urgent and include sufficient detail for us to assess and respond promptly.\n\n## 5. Contact\n\nLaw enforcement and regulatory enquiries: **support@omaya.io** (subject line: Law Enforcement Request).\n\n---\n\n*We may update these guidelines from time to time.*\n","OMAYA-Payment-Policy-v1.1.md":"# Payment Policy\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThis Payment Policy describes how payments, settlements, fees, and refunds are handled on **OMAYA.io** services operated by **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (\"**OMAYA**\").\n\n---\n\n## 1. Supported Payment Methods\n\nAvailable payment methods depend on your region, product, and verification status. We support approved local payment providers and digital asset networks as shown on the Platform at the time of your transaction.\n\n## 2. Fees and Charges\n\nApplicable fees, spreads, and charges are disclosed before you confirm a transaction. Fees may vary based on payment method, asset, network conditions, and regulatory requirements.\n\n## 3. Settlement and Timing\n\nSettlement times depend on the payment method, network confirmations, compliance review, and partner processing. We are not responsible for delays caused by third-party banks or networks outside our control.\n\n## 4. Refunds and Disputes\n\nRefund eligibility is assessed case-by-case in line with our Terms of Service and AML requirements. Contact support promptly if you believe a transaction was processed incorrectly.\n\n## 5. Compliance Holds\n\nWe may delay, reject, or reverse transactions where required for AML/KYC review, sanctions screening, fraud prevention, or legal obligations.\n\n---\n\n*This Payment Policy is incorporated into our Terms of Service.*\n","OMAYA-Referral-Program-Terms-v1.1.md":"# Referral Program Terms\n\n**OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE**\n\n**Effective Date:** 31 May 2026  \n**Last Updated:** 31 May 2026  \n**Version:** 1.1\n\n---\n\nThese Referral Program Terms apply when you participate in referral, reward, or incentive programmes offered by **OMAYA EXPRESS EXCHANGE** (trading as **OMAYA.io**). They supplement our **Terms of Service**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Eligibility\n\nParticipation may require a verified account in good standing. We may restrict participation by region, product, or user type.\n\n## 2. Referral Rewards\n\nReward amounts, currencies, and payout timing are shown in the programme materials on the Platform. We may change or withdraw programmes at any time.\n\n## 3. Prohibited Conduct\n\nSelf-referrals, duplicate accounts, fake identities, automated abuse, or any attempt to manipulate the programme may result in forfeiture of rewards and account action.\n\n## 4. Tax and Compliance\n\nYou are responsible for any taxes on rewards. Rewards may be withheld pending AML/KYC or fraud review.\n\n## 5. Programme Changes\n\nWe may amend, suspend, or end referral programmes without prior notice where permitted by law. Continued participation after changes constitutes acceptance of updated terms.\n\n---\n\n*By participating in a referral programme, you agree to these terms and our Terms of Service.*\n"};
